     "xbtro_instance": "mo_policy(): over the observation configuration of this body model, generate candidate changes, cost each (set-up time, apparatus perturbation as a vector), choose among the non-dominated ones, apply, measure the actual identifiability gain and the actual perturbation of the body, and retract a change that proves to perturb what it observes. Reach is reported as a vector."
    },
    "MS": {
     "not_covered": "physical flows other than this body's; reallocation while running (paths are compared across runs); latency/energy of real hardware",
     "repository_status": "NOT IMPLEMENTED",
     "xbtro_instance": "ms_paths(): executable alternatives (sets of operation lines, Xeno-14 conditions, a stopped response) are run for one stated consequence; each is measured on latency, energy, information gain, intervention reach time, reconstruction cost and recovery time, kept as a vector; the non-dominated set is reported; a choice is made only under constraints stated by the caller. The stopped response is one of the paths."
    },
    "ZCA": {
     "not_covered": "no global registry, no address equivalence (no 'same object' function), no content-hash identity, no address resolution, no Concept Address Layer",
